  "sourceId": "thinksr",
  "title": "ThinkSR: compact thought, dense output",
  "lang": "en",
  "scenes": [
    {
      "id": "s01-flow",
      "intent": "The recurrence returns to the DQ-CTM thought stage, while the rest of the image pipeline stays linear.",
      "claim": "ThinkSR runs end to end through encoder, windows, shared DQ-CTM ticks, and decoder.",
      "narration": "The image first becomes a dense carrier, so later stages still have spatial detail to work with. Windowing prepares local token groups without leaving the carrier behind. The compact DQ-CTM process repeats inside its own stage, using shared parameters across ticks. The decoder turns the updated dense carrier back into the super-resolved image.",
