    {
      "id": "s02-carrier",
      "intent": "The equation first makes a dense feature field from the low-resolution image, then partitions that field into window tokens without discarding it.",
      "claim": "The carrier equation is \\mathbf{F}=\\mathcal{E}(\\mathbf{I}_{\\mathrm{LR}}),\\qquad \\mathbf{X}=\\mathcal{W}(\\mathbf{F}).",
      "narration": "The low-resolution image is the input to the encoder, not directly to the thought process. The encoder produces a dense feature field named F. The window operator then partitions that same field. X names the windowed tokens that carry all positions forward.",
